// Title: RDP Connection Allowed Via Netsh.EXE
// ID: 01aeb693-138d-49d2-9403-c4f52d7d3d62
// Status: test
// Level: high
// Author: Sander Wiebing
// Date: 2020-05-23
// Tags: attack.defense-impairment, attack.t1686.003
// Description: Detects usage of the netsh command to open and allow connections to port 3389 (RDP). As seen used by Sarwent Malware
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

process where (((process.command_line like "*_firewall *" and process.command_line like "*_add *" and process.command_line like "*_tcp *" and process.command_line like "*_3389*") and (process.command_line like "*_portopening*" or process.command_line like "*_allow*")) and ((process.executable endswith "\\netsh.exe") or (process.pe.original_file_name == "netsh.exe")))
